1
00:00:46,281 --> 00:00:50,240
These are times
dark, without a doubt.

2
00:00:50,852 --> 00:00:56,484
Our world has never faced
such a big threat.

3
00:00:57,458 --> 00:01:01,417
But I tell you this
to the citizens:

4
00:01:01,596 --> 00:01:05,498
We, always at your service...

5
00:01:05,667 --> 00:01:08,329
...we will continue defending
your freedom...

6
00:01:08,503 --> 00:01:12,837
...and repelling the forces
who seek to take it away!

7
00:01:14,042 --> 00:01:19,309
His Ministry remains...

8
00:01:19,847 --> 00:01:21,815
...strong.

9
00:01:24,986 --> 00:01:27,978
DARK MARK
GENERATE PANIC

10
00:01:28,156 --> 00:01:29,851
THE PROPHET

11
00:01:30,024 --> 00:01:31,924
VIOLENCE SPREADS
MUGGLE FAMILY MURDERED

12
00:01:32,093 --> 00:01:33,583
NUMBER OF DEATH EAERS INCREASES

13
00:01:39,167 --> 00:01:41,362
Hermione! The tea is ready!

14
00:01:41,536 --> 00:01:43,470
I'm coming, mom!

15
00:01:47,408 --> 00:01:49,308
Come on, Dudley! Hurry up!

16
00:01:49,477 --> 00:01:52,503
I don't understand why
we have to go.

17
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:57,447
We are no longer safe here.

18
00:02:12,834 --> 00:02:17,203
Ron! Tell your dad
that dinner is ready!

19
00:02:22,210 --> 00:02:23,939
Is the show about Australia?

20
00:02:24,579 --> 00:02:26,069
It's wonderful, isn't it?

21
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:33,944
<i>Obliviate.</i>

22
00:03:42,423 --> 00:03:49,261
HARRY POTTER AND THE HALLOWS
OF DEATH PART 1

23
00:04:48,289 --> 00:04:49,950
Severus.

24
00:04:50,124 --> 00:04:53,491
I was worried that
you would have been lost.

25
00:04:53,661 --> 00:04:57,119
Come, we'll save you a seat.

26
00:05:01,569 --> 00:05:02,900
You bring news, I hope?

27
00:05:03,070 --> 00:05:06,733
It's going to happen next Saturday
at dusk.

28
00:05:06,908 --> 00:05:09,274
I have other information, Sir.

29
00:05:09,443 --> 00:05:12,571
Dawlish, the auror,
He said that the Potter boy...

30
00:05:12,747 --> 00:05:15,841
...will not be transferred
until the 30th of this month.

31
00:05:16,284 --> 00:05:17,546
The day before turning 17 years old.

32
00:05:17,718 --> 00:05:20,949
It's a red herring.

33
00:05:21,622 --> 00:05:25,786
The Auror Office
He no longer protects Harry Potter.

34
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:30,329
His relatives believe that we
We infiltrated the Ministry.

35
00:05:30,932 --> 00:05:33,400
Well, they are right, right?

36
00:05:37,004 --> 00:05:39,472
What do you say, Pius?

37
00:05:43,010 --> 00:05:45,604
One hears many things, Lord.

38
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:49,079
It is not clear whether the truth
is among them.

39
00:05:49,517 --> 00:05:51,883
Said like a good politician.

40
00:05:52,053 --> 00:05:55,113
You are going to be very useful to us, Pius.

41
00:05:58,726 --> 00:06:01,957
-Where are they going to take the boy?
-To a safe house.

42
00:06:02,363 --> 00:06:04,991
Probably the one of
a member of the Order.

43
00:06:05,166 --> 00:06:08,397
They say that it has been given
the greatest possible protection.

44
00:06:08,569 --> 00:06:12,505
since it's there
it will be impractical to attack him.

45
00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:17,372
Sir, I would like to offer myself
for this work.

46
00:06:17,545 --> 00:06:18,842
I want to kill
to the boy.

47
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:20,204
Wormtail!

48
00:06:21,182 --> 00:06:24,151
I told you to shut up
to our guests!

49
00:06:24,318 --> 00:06:26,218
Yes, Lord.

50
00:06:26,387 --> 00:06:29,049
Right away, sir.

51
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:33,784
Your thirst for blood
It's inspiring, Bellatrix...

52
00:06:34,228 --> 00:06:37,527
...but I must kill
to Harry Potter.

53
00:06:40,001 --> 00:06:44,802
But there is a complication
unfortunate.

54
00:06:44,972 --> 00:06:50,171
My wand and Potter's
They share the same core.

55
00:06:51,412 --> 00:06:57,976
In a sense they are twins.

56
00:06:58,152 --> 00:07:02,851
We can hurt each other,
but not fatally.

57
00:07:04,458 --> 00:07:07,256
If I have to kill him...

58
00:07:07,929 --> 00:07:11,695
...I must do it
with another's wand.

59
00:07:13,701 --> 00:07:19,401
Surely one of you
He wants the honor.

60
00:07:24,378 --> 00:07:29,179
How about you, Lucius?

61
00:07:31,686 --> 00:07:33,085
Sir?

62
00:07:33,254 --> 00:07:35,222
''Sir?''

63
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:39,919
I require your wand.

64
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:55,708
Do I detect elm?

65
00:07:55,876 --> 00:07:57,844
Yes, Lord.

66
00:08:03,784 --> 00:08:06,719
And the core?

67
00:08:06,887 --> 00:08:08,684
Dragon

68
00:08:09,256 --> 00:08:10,883
Dragon heart, Lord.

69
00:08:11,058 --> 00:08:13,458
Dragon heart.

70
00:08:28,976 --> 00:08:33,572
For those who don't know, we
accompanied by Miss Charity Burbage...

71
00:08:33,748 --> 00:08:39,243
...which until recently taught
at Hogwarts School of Magic.

72
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:44,050
His specialty was
Muggle Studies.

73
00:08:46,093 --> 00:08:52,362
Miss Burbage thinks the
Muggles are similar to us.

74
00:08:52,533 --> 00:08:56,162
She would like it, if she sent...

75
00:08:56,937 --> 00:08:58,871
...that we would mate with them.

76
00:09:02,543 --> 00:09:08,743
Think about mixing the two
blood is not an abomination...

77
00:09:08,916 --> 00:09:11,942
...but something we should encourage.

78
00:09:13,020 --> 00:09:14,885
Severus.

79
00:09:15,056 --> 00:09:17,024
Severus, please.

80
00:09:18,692 --> 00:09:20,853
We are friends.

81
00:09:25,633 --> 00:09:27,191
<i>Avada Kedavra!</i>

82
00:09:37,445 --> 00:09:39,470
Nagini.

83
00:09:43,084 --> 00:09:44,745
Dinner

84
00:10:31,432 --> 00:10:34,026
REMEMBERING DUMBLEDORE

85
00:11:30,057 --> 00:11:33,390
Hello, Harry!

86
00:11:33,594 --> 00:11:34,720
Wow! Hello!

87
00:11:34,895 --> 00:11:37,796
-You look healthy.
-Yes, he is an adonis.

88
00:11:37,965 --> 00:11:40,433
Let's go hide
before they kill him.

89
00:11:40,601 --> 00:11:41,625
Good night.

90
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:48,940
Don't you take care of the prime minister?

91
00:11:49,109 --> 00:11:51,009
You are more important.

92
00:11:51,178 --> 00:11:54,238
-Hello, Harry. Bill Weasley.
-Nice to meet you.

93
00:11:54,415 --> 00:11:57,407
-He wasn't so handsome before.
-He was very ugly.

94
00:11:57,585 --> 00:11:58,984
It's true.

95
00:11:59,153 --> 00:12:01,678
I owe this to
a werewolf, Greyback.

96
00:12:01,855 --> 00:12:05,222
-One day I will repay the favor.
-To me you are beautiful, William.

97
00:12:05,593 --> 00:12:09,222
Just remember that now
He likes raw steaks.

98
00:12:09,396 --> 00:12:11,728
My husband, the joker.

99
00:12:11,899 --> 00:12:15,164
By the way, I have news.
Remus and I...

100
00:12:15,336 --> 00:12:17,770
Enough! Then we
we update.

101
00:12:17,938 --> 00:12:20,907
We have to get out
from here! And soon!

102
00:12:21,575 --> 00:12:24,840
You are a minor,
you still have the Detector.

103
00:12:25,012 --> 00:12:26,036
What is the Detector?

104
00:12:26,213 --> 00:12:28,875
If you sneeze,
The Ministry finds out.

105
00:12:29,049 --> 00:12:32,212
We have to use a medium
undetectable transport:

106
00:12:32,386 --> 00:12:34,718
Brooms, thestrals and the like.
We will go in pairs.

107
00:12:34,888 --> 00:12:38,654
If there's someone outside waiting for us,
which is very likely...

108
00:12:38,826 --> 00:12:41,317
...they won't know which Harry Potter
is the real one.

109
00:12:41,762 --> 00:12:42,922
The real one?

110
00:12:44,265 --> 00:12:47,359
I think you know
this particular potion.

111
00:12:47,534 --> 00:12:49,832
No. For no reason.

112
00:12:50,004 --> 00:12:51,335
I told you he was going to refuse.

113
00:12:51,505 --> 00:12:54,633
If you think I will allow
to risk their lives for me...

114
00:12:54,808 --> 00:12:57,868
-We've never done it, right?
-No. This is different.

115
00:12:58,045 --> 00:13:00,036
Take that, become like me. No!

116
00:13:00,214 --> 00:13:02,045
Nobody loves the idea.

117
00:13:02,216 --> 00:13:06,380
If something goes wrong, we stay
weaklings with glasses.

118
00:13:06,553 --> 00:13:08,214
Everyone here is of legal age.

119
00:13:08,956 --> 00:13:11,550
Everyone agreed
to take the risk.

120
00:13:11,725 --> 00:13:14,626
Technically, they forced me.

121
00:13:14,795 --> 00:13:16,990
Mundungus Fletcher, Mr. Potter.

122
00:13:17,164 --> 00:13:19,724
-A great admirer of yours.
-Shut up, Mundungus!

123
00:13:21,035 --> 00:13:23,526
Well, Granger, let's get to work.

124
00:13:23,704 --> 00:13:26,434
-Damn it, Hermione!
-Directly here, please.

125
00:13:36,283 --> 00:13:40,481
I warn everyone who never
have taken Polyjuice Potion:

126
00:13:40,654 --> 00:13:42,281
It tastes like elf pee.

127
00:13:42,456 --> 00:13:45,425
Do you have a lot of experience with that?

128
00:13:46,327 --> 00:13:49,262
I just wanted to reduce the tension.

129
00:14:21,195 --> 00:14:23,254
-We are identical!
-We are identical!

130
00:14:23,430 --> 00:14:24,488
Not yet.

131
00:14:28,168 --> 00:14:30,728
Don't you have something more elegant?

132
00:14:30,904 --> 00:14:32,371
I don't love this color.

133
00:14:32,539 --> 00:14:35,337
Let's see if you love this:
you are not you. Get undressed.

134
00:14:35,509 --> 00:14:38,808
-Okay!
-You also need to change.

135
00:14:39,313 --> 00:14:41,941
Don't look at me. I look horrible.

136
00:14:42,116 --> 00:14:44,414
I knew he lied about the tattoo.

137
00:14:44,585 --> 00:14:47,019
Harry, you really are blind.

138
00:14:47,187 --> 00:14:50,884
Let's form pairs.
Each Potter will have a protector.

139
00:14:51,058 --> 00:14:54,357
Mundungus, don't separate me.
I want to watch you.

140
00:14:54,895 --> 00:14:56,726
-As for Harry...
-Yes?

141
00:14:57,564 --> 00:14:58,963
The real one.

142
00:14:59,133 --> 00:15:01,499
-Where the hell are you?
-Here.

143
00:15:01,668 --> 00:15:03,636
You're going with Hagrid.

144
00:15:03,804 --> 00:15:08,832
I brought you here 16 years ago when
You were smaller than a bowtruckle.

145
00:15:09,009 --> 00:15:11,910
It's me who
must get you out of here.

146
00:15:12,079 --> 00:15:15,014
Yes, how touching. Let's go!

147
00:15:28,328 --> 00:15:32,230
Head to the Burrow.
See you there.

148
00:15:35,002 --> 00:15:36,731
Hold on tight, Harry!

149
00:15:36,904 --> 00:15:38,701
One!

150
00:15:39,573 --> 00:15:41,370
Two!

151
00:15:47,781 --> 00:15:49,578
Three!

152
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:22,743
-Follow us!
-Where are you?

153
00:16:23,951 --> 00:16:25,680
It's on your right!

154
00:16:25,853 --> 00:16:27,480
There, now!

155
00:16:27,654 --> 00:16:29,315
Down!

156
00:16:34,795 --> 00:16:36,456
We have to help others!

157
00:16:36,864 --> 00:16:39,765
I can't! Mad-Eye's orders!

158
00:16:46,707 --> 00:16:48,504
Hold on!

159
00:16:52,312 --> 00:16:54,371
<i>Fainting!</i>

160
00:17:08,095 --> 00:17:09,187
Hold on tight, Harry!

161
00:17:19,106 --> 00:17:20,971
Hagrid!

162
00:17:38,191 --> 00:17:40,455
No. No.

163
00:18:02,549 --> 00:18:04,540
<i>Harry.</i>

164
00:19:24,498 --> 00:19:27,558
Harry. Hagrid.

165
00:19:28,969 --> 00:19:32,427
What happened?
Where are the others?

166
00:19:32,606 --> 00:19:33,766
Has no one returned?

167
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:37,501
They fell on us right away.
There was no escape.

168
00:19:37,678 --> 00:19:40,841
Thank God you are well.

169
00:19:41,014 --> 00:19:43,574
They were waiting for us.
It was an ambush.

170
00:19:43,750 --> 00:19:46,150
Ron and Tonks should already
be here

171
00:19:46,319 --> 00:19:47,513
Dad and Fred too.

172
00:19:50,457 --> 00:19:52,118
Here!

173
00:19:52,759 --> 00:19:56,195
Soon! Let's go inside!

174
00:19:59,866 --> 00:20:01,925
Oh, my son!

175
00:20:07,474 --> 00:20:09,499
-Lupin!
-What are you doing?

176
00:20:12,045 --> 00:20:14,980
What creature sat
in the corner...

177
00:20:15,148 --> 00:20:18,447
...the first time Harry Potter
Did you visit my office at Hogwarts?

178
00:20:18,618 --> 00:20:20,245
-Are you crazy?
-What creature?

179
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:22,251
A grindilow.

180
00:20:28,595 --> 00:20:30,256
They betrayed us.

181
00:20:30,430 --> 00:20:32,830
Voldemort knew about your transfer.

182
00:20:32,999 --> 00:20:35,900
I had to check
that you were not an imposter.

183
00:20:43,043 --> 00:20:44,476
Wait!

184
00:20:47,481 --> 00:20:52,009
The last words that Albus
Dumbledore told us both?

185
00:20:53,820 --> 00:20:58,189
''Harry is our best
hope. Trust him."

186
00:21:02,729 --> 00:21:03,821
What gave you away?

187
00:21:03,997 --> 00:21:07,194
I think Hedwig.
He was trying to protect me.

188
00:21:23,750 --> 00:21:24,910
Thank you.

189
00:21:25,085 --> 00:21:27,246
He deserves it. It was brilliant.

190
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:30,514
-I wouldn't be here if it weren't for him.
-Really?

191
00:21:31,525 --> 00:21:34,187
It always surprises you.

192
00:21:42,402 --> 00:21:43,596
Are we the last?

193
00:21:44,905 --> 00:21:45,929
Where's George?

194
00:22:07,227 --> 00:22:09,457
How do you feel, Georgie?

195
00:22:11,464 --> 00:22:12,988
Cardinal.

196
00:22:14,201 --> 00:22:15,429
How do you say?

197
00:22:16,369 --> 00:22:19,930
Cardinal.

198
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:23,500
Because it came out cardinal red.
You understand?

199
00:22:25,312 --> 00:22:30,011
There are lots of jokes about ears
and you come out with ''cardinalicio''.

200
00:22:30,183 --> 00:22:31,343
How pathetic.

201
00:22:31,952 --> 00:22:34,250
I'm still more handsome than you.

202
00:22:37,791 --> 00:22:39,986
Mad-Eye is dead.

203
00:22:50,370 --> 00:22:54,101
Mundungus looked at Voldemort.
and disappeared.

204
00:23:17,030 --> 00:23:19,055
<i>Go to the Burrow!</i>

205
00:23:19,866 --> 00:23:21,925
<i>-It's worse than I imagined.
-Seven?</i>

206
00:23:22,102 --> 00:23:24,036
<i>Seven? A horcrux.</i>

207
00:23:24,204 --> 00:23:28,004
<i>-They can be anywhere.
-Break the soul into seven pieces...</i>

208
00:23:28,174 --> 00:23:31,143
<i>-What if you destroy the 7 horcruxes?
-You destroy Voldemort.</i>

209
00:23:34,748 --> 00:23:36,375
<i>Trust me.</i>

210
00:23:37,317 --> 00:23:41,651
<i>You lied to me.
You lied to me, Ollivander.</i>

211
00:24:12,819 --> 00:24:14,753
Where are you going?

212
00:24:18,425 --> 00:24:22,521
Nobody else is going to die. Not for me.

213
00:24:22,696 --> 00:24:24,493
For you?

214
00:24:24,664 --> 00:24:26,894
Did Mad-Eye die for you?

215
00:24:27,067 --> 00:24:30,002
Did George suffer the curse for you?

216
00:24:30,770 --> 00:24:34,706
You may be the Chosen One, but
This is much bigger than that.

217
00:24:34,874 --> 00:24:37,399
It has always been bigger.

218
00:24:39,612 --> 00:24:42,103
-Come with me.
-And leave Hermione?

219
00:24:42,582 --> 00:24:46,814
Are you crazy? we wouldn't last
not even two days without her.

220
00:24:48,221 --> 00:24:49,745
Don't tell him I said that.

221
00:24:51,324 --> 00:24:54,521
Also, you still have the Detector.

222
00:24:54,694 --> 00:24:58,790
-And there's still the wedding.
-I don't care about a wedding.

223
00:24:58,965 --> 00:25:03,834
Forgive me. It doesn't matter whose it is.
I have to look for those horcruxes.

224
00:25:04,004 --> 00:25:05,972
They are our only possibility
to defeat him.

225
00:25:06,139 --> 00:25:09,108
The longer we are here,
the stronger it gets.

226
00:25:10,543 --> 00:25:12,636
Not tonight.

227
00:25:12,946 --> 00:25:15,414
We would do you a favor.

228
00:25:43,176 --> 00:25:45,110
Do you think he knows?

229
00:25:45,845 --> 00:25:51,715
I mean, they're pieces.
of his soul, the horcruxes.

230
00:25:52,452 --> 00:25:56,718
When Dumbledore destroyed the ring
and you, Tom Riddle's Diary...

231
00:25:58,224 --> 00:26:00,818
...he must have felt something.

232
00:26:01,594 --> 00:26:05,325
To kill the other horcruxes
we have to find them.

233
00:26:05,698 --> 00:26:07,666
Where are they?

234
00:26:08,201 --> 00:26:10,260
Where do we start?

235
00:26:13,706 --> 00:26:14,798
Ready when you

236
00:26:14,974 --> 00:26:16,373
Bill and Fleur

237
00:26:16,543 --> 00:26:20,843
Pay attention!
It's his brother's wedding! Cheer up!

238
00:26:21,014 --> 00:26:23,744
DUMBLEDORE SECRETS REVEALED

239
00:26:23,917 --> 00:26:26,181
RITA SKEETER RELEASES NEW BOOK

240
00:26:38,765 --> 00:26:44,032
REMEMBERING DUMBLEDORE
BY ELPHIAS DOGE

241
00:26:46,272 --> 00:26:48,331
Can you zip me up?

242
00:27:02,188 --> 00:27:04,122
It seems ridiculous, doesn't it?
A wedding.

243
00:27:04,624 --> 00:27:06,990
Given what's happening.

244
00:27:08,328 --> 00:27:10,387
Maybe it's the best reason
to do it...

245
00:27:10,997 --> 00:27:13,522
...for what is happening.

246
00:27:29,582 --> 00:27:31,743
Good morning.

247
00:27:44,764 --> 00:27:46,425
All together!

248
00:27:46,599 --> 00:27:52,037
One! Two! Three!

249
00:28:02,115 --> 00:28:04,549
How's that side going, guys?

250
00:28:05,185 --> 00:28:07,119
-Fantastic!
-Fantastic!

251
00:28:09,222 --> 00:28:14,057
Damn. What are you doing here
the minister of magic?

252
00:28:19,966 --> 00:28:21,831
To what do we owe
the pleasure, minister?

253
00:28:22,001 --> 00:28:26,563
We both know the answer
to that question, Mr. Potter.

254
00:28:34,247 --> 00:28:36,147
And that is...?

255
00:28:44,190 --> 00:28:48,092
''This is the last
will and testament...

256
