-This is complete madness.
-Complete.

511
00:51:19,744 --> 00:51:21,769
The world is crazy.

512
00:51:21,947 --> 00:51:23,380
Go ahead.

513
00:51:23,982 --> 00:51:26,416
We have to look for a horcrux.

514
00:51:48,540 --> 00:51:52,101
KNIGHTS

515
00:52:20,305 --> 00:52:22,705
We enter releasing the water.

516
00:52:26,745 --> 00:52:29,509
That's disgusting.

517
00:53:00,512 --> 00:53:02,036
You! Come!

518
00:53:02,213 --> 00:53:04,374
-What? That?
-Come on.

519
00:53:04,549 --> 00:53:06,983
-What did I do?
-Keep walking.

520
00:53:14,359 --> 00:53:16,293
-Are they...?
-Muggles.

521
00:53:16,461 --> 00:53:21,057
In its proper place.

522
00:53:22,834 --> 00:53:26,031
The truth is, I am
starting to scare me.

523
00:53:28,306 --> 00:53:32,800
How long did you say it was going
How long will this Polyjuice Potion last?

524
00:53:33,344 --> 00:53:35,539
I didn't say it.

525
00:53:41,553 --> 00:53:43,487
Cattermole.

526
00:53:44,522 --> 00:53:48,117
It's still raining inside
my office. It's been two days.

527
00:53:50,061 --> 00:53:51,824
Have you tried an umbrella?

528
00:53:52,797 --> 00:53:55,732
You know I'm going down,
Right, Cattermole?

529
00:53:56,301 --> 00:54:00,260
-Down?
-To interrogate your wife.

530
00:54:01,172 --> 00:54:05,108
If the purity of blood of
my wife was in doubt...

531
00:54:05,276 --> 00:54:08,177
...and the head of Magical Security
asked me a favor...

532
00:54:08,346 --> 00:54:13,909
...I think maybe I would give it priority.

533
00:54:14,486 --> 00:54:16,681
You have one hour.

534
00:54:28,433 --> 00:54:34,099
Oh my god! What am I going to do?
My wife is downstairs, alone!

535
00:54:34,405 --> 00:54:38,671
-Ron, you don't have a wife.
-Oh, that's true.

536
00:54:38,843 --> 00:54:40,811
<i>Level 2.</i>

537
00:54:41,613 --> 00:54:43,740
How do I make it stop raining?

538
00:54:43,915 --> 00:54:46,509
<i>Try Finite Incantatem.</i>

539
00:54:46,684 --> 00:54:50,142
<i>Department of Magical Security
and the Misuse of Magic.</i>

540
00:54:50,321 --> 00:54:52,289
This is your level, Ron.

541
00:54:56,528 --> 00:55:01,363
<i>Finite Incantatem. OK.
What if that doesn't work...?</i>

542
00:55:13,278 --> 00:55:16,213
<i>Level 1, Ministry of Magic
and Support Personnel.</i>

543
00:55:16,381 --> 00:55:18,508
If we don't find Umbridge
in one hour...

544
00:55:18,683 --> 00:55:20,674
...let's go get Ron
and we return another day.

545
00:55:20,852 --> 00:55:21,876
-Okay?
-Yeah.

546
00:55:25,456 --> 00:55:27,788
Ah, Mafalda.
Travers sent you, right?

547
00:55:27,959 --> 00:55:31,019
How good.
Let's go straight down.

548
00:55:33,364 --> 00:55:35,889
Albert, aren't you going out?

549
00:56:01,292 --> 00:56:03,089
MUDBLOODS AND THE DANGER

550
00:56:03,261 --> 00:56:04,990
FOR THE PURE BLOOD

551
00:56:09,267 --> 00:56:11,292
Runcorn.

552
00:56:18,176 --> 00:56:21,009
DOLORES UMBRIDGE
DEPUTY SECRETARY OF THE MINISTER

553
00:56:22,480 --> 00:56:24,675
MUGGLEBORN REGISTRATION

554
00:57:03,788 --> 00:57:05,187
<i>Accio locket!</i>

555
00:57:25,143 --> 00:57:27,043
WHEN THE MUGGLES ATTACK

556
00:57:35,353 --> 00:57:36,911
MUGGLEBORN REGISTRATION

557
00:57:46,831 --> 00:57:48,389
TRACKING VERY HIGH RISK

558
00:57:54,105 --> 00:57:57,438
MESTIZO
MEMBER ORDER OF THE PHOENIX

559
00:57:59,877 --> 00:58:03,040
Good. Calm down, okay?

560
00:58:03,948 --> 00:58:06,416
Get to work, please.

561
00:58:07,218 --> 00:58:09,049
Calm down.

562
00:58:14,392 --> 00:58:16,087
Runcorn.

563
00:58:23,901 --> 00:58:25,664
Good morning.

564
00:58:27,372 --> 00:58:29,806
Ron. It's me.

565
00:58:29,974 --> 00:58:33,808
Harry! Damn, I forgot
how you looked

566
00:58:33,978 --> 00:58:35,411
Where is Hermione?

567
00:58:35,580 --> 00:58:39,311
He went down to the courts,
with Umbridge.

568
00:58:45,857 --> 00:58:47,984
It's very cold down here.

569
00:58:48,159 --> 00:58:51,754
I am of mixed blood.
My father was a magician.

570
00:58:51,929 --> 00:58:54,261
William Alderton.
He worked here 30 years.

571
00:58:54,432 --> 00:58:57,868
Maybe he knew him.
He always put his jacket on backwards.

572
00:58:58,036 --> 00:59:00,504
There has been an error!
I am a mestizo!

573
00:59:00,671 --> 00:59:03,868
We have to go back!
I am a mestizo!

574
00:59:13,985 --> 00:59:16,078
-Mary Elizabeth Cattermole?
-Yeah.

575
00:59:16,254 --> 00:59:21,191
From Chislehurst Gardens 27,
Great Tolling, Evesham?

576
00:59:21,359 --> 00:59:22,383
-Yes.
-It's here.

577
00:59:22,560 --> 00:59:27,361
Mother of Maisie, Ellie and Alfred?
Reginald's wife?

578
00:59:31,569 --> 00:59:32,627
Reg?

579
00:59:44,215 --> 00:59:46,046
Thanks, Albert.

580
00:59:48,653 --> 00:59:51,383
Mary Elizabeth Cattermole?

581
00:59:53,591 --> 00:59:54,649
Yes.

582
00:59:55,693 --> 00:59:59,220
Today they took a wand from him
upon arriving at the Ministry.

583
00:59:59,397 --> 01:00:02,161
Is this the wand?

584
01:00:04,001 --> 01:00:08,529
Can you tell us which wizard
did you take his wand?

585
01:00:08,706 --> 01:00:11,140
I didn't take it from anyone.

586
01:00:12,376 --> 01:00:18,178
I bought it in Callejón Diagón,
at Ollivanders when I was 11 years old.

587
01:00:19,617 --> 01:00:22,108
The wand chose me.

588
01:00:23,488 --> 01:00:25,251
Lie.

589
01:00:25,690 --> 01:00:30,252
Wands only choose witches
and you are not a witch.

590
01:00:30,428 --> 01:00:32,453
Yes, I am.

591
01:00:32,897 --> 01:00:35,957
Tell them, Reg. Tell them what I am.

592
01:00:38,503 --> 01:00:39,868
Reg, tell them.

593
01:00:49,847 --> 01:00:51,610
What are you doing, Albert?

594
01:00:54,519 --> 01:00:56,419
You lie, Dolores.

595
01:00:58,789 --> 01:01:01,349
And one should not lie.

596
01:01:02,160 --> 01:01:03,457
<i>Fainting!</i>

597
01:01:11,169 --> 01:01:12,534
It's Harry Potter!

598
01:01:12,703 --> 01:01:15,171
It's going to be a good anecdote
for the children.

599
01:01:31,189 --> 01:01:32,349
<i>Expecto Patronum!</i>

600
01:01:58,816 --> 01:02:00,841
Mary, go home.

601
01:02:02,286 --> 01:02:03,753
Get the kids together.

602
01:02:03,921 --> 01:02:07,288
See you there. we have to
leave the country, you understand?

603
01:02:07,458 --> 01:02:09,926
Mary, do as I tell you.

604
01:02:24,342 --> 01:02:25,502
Mary?

605
01:02:27,144 --> 01:02:29,044
Who is he?

606
01:02:30,181 --> 01:02:33,173
It's a long story.
Nice to meet you.

607
01:02:33,351 --> 01:02:34,716
It's Harry Potter!

608
01:02:35,419 --> 01:02:37,387
It's Harry! Harry Potter!

609
01:02:37,555 --> 01:02:39,750
After him!
Grab it!

610
01:02:39,924 --> 01:02:41,858
-Quick!
-Stop it!

611
01:03:15,693 --> 01:03:17,524
<i>Expelliarmus!</i>

612
01:04:04,975 --> 01:04:06,966
Oh my god.

613
01:04:12,249 --> 01:04:15,514
Harry! Soon, in my bag!

614
01:04:15,686 --> 01:04:18,211
There is a bottle, ''Essence of Dictamo''.

615
01:04:23,761 --> 01:04:26,457
Hurry up!

616
01:04:27,231 --> 01:04:29,324
<i>Accio dictamo!</i>

617
01:04:29,700 --> 01:04:32,430
Quiet. Uncover it.

618
01:04:32,603 --> 01:04:34,093
Hermione, his arm!

619
01:04:34,271 --> 01:04:36,262
I know, do it!

620
01:04:37,007 --> 01:04:38,736
It's okay.

621
01:04:40,010 --> 01:04:43,969
-It's going to burn a little.
-What happened? I thought we were going...

622
01:04:44,148 --> 01:04:46,878
-...to go to Grimmauld Place.
-That's how it is.

623
01:04:47,051 --> 01:04:48,882
One more, one more!

624
01:04:49,053 --> 01:04:53,581
We were there, but...
Yaxley had a hold on me and...

625
01:04:53,758 --> 01:04:56,784
I had seen us
and we couldn't stay there!

626
01:04:56,961 --> 01:05:00,089
I brought us here...

627
01:05:00,564 --> 01:05:03,192
...but Ron suffered a split.

628
01:05:06,270 --> 01:05:08,067
Quiet.

629
01:05:27,124 --> 01:05:29,490
<i>Protego Totalum.</i>

630
01:05:30,961 --> 01:05:32,428
<i>Salvio Hexia.</i>

631
01:05:32,596 --> 01:05:33,995
What are you doing?

632
01:05:34,165 --> 01:05:36,463
Protective charms.

633
01:05:36,634 --> 01:05:40,229
I don't want another visit like
the one on Shaftesbury Avenue.

634
01:05:40,404 --> 01:05:42,099
Start erecting the tent.

635
01:05:42,773 --> 01:05:44,604
<i>-The store?
-Protego Totalum.</i>

636
01:05:44,775 --> 01:05:46,902
Where will I find a store?

637
01:05:47,077 --> 01:05:51,377
<i>Repello Muggletum. Muffliato.</i>

638
01:06:01,692 --> 01:06:03,592
You first.

639
01:06:06,597 --> 01:06:08,690
<i>Dissendium!</i>

640
01:06:22,313 --> 01:06:24,213
<i>Fire!</i>

641
01:06:29,620 --> 01:06:31,645
<i>Expulsion!</i>

642
01:06:38,863 --> 01:06:40,990
<i>Diffindo!</i>

643
01:06:42,433 --> 01:06:43,457
<i>Reducto!</i>

644
01:07:04,889 --> 01:07:06,754
What are you doing?

645
01:07:08,158 --> 01:07:10,922
We have to save it
until we figure out how to destroy it.

646
01:07:11,095 --> 01:07:13,791
It seems strange to me, comrade.
Dumbledore sends you...

647
01:07:13,964 --> 01:07:17,730
...to look for horcruxes,
but it doesn't tell you how to destroy them.

648
01:07:17,902 --> 01:07:19,529
Doesn't that bother you?

649
01:07:31,916 --> 01:07:35,317
<i>An elf named Gornuk
He was also murdered.</i>

650
01:07:35,486 --> 01:07:38,546
<i>Dean Thomas, Muggle-born
and a second elf...</i>

651
01:07:38,722 --> 01:07:41,657
<i>...both traveling with Tonks,
Cresswell and Gornuk...</i>

652
01:07:41,825 --> 01:07:43,349
<i>...maybe they escaped.</i>

653
01:07:43,527 --> 01:07:47,293
<i>If Dean is listening
or if anyone knows his whereabouts...</i>

654
01:07:47,464 --> 01:07:50,524
<i>...his family is desperate
for news.</i>

655
01:07:50,701 --> 01:07:54,068
<i>In Gadley, they found murdered
to a family of five.</i>

656
01:07:54,238 --> 01:07:57,503
<i>You know the spell, Harry.</i>

657
01:08:01,245 --> 01:08:02,507
<i>Tell me.</i>

658
01:08:05,149 --> 01:08:06,980
<i>Tell me, Gregorovitch.</i>

659
01:08:07,151 --> 01:08:08,778
They stole it from me!

660
01:08:08,953 --> 01:08:12,411
Who was it? The thief?

661
01:08:15,559 --> 01:08:19,518
<i>It was a boy.
He was the one who took her.</i>

662
01:08:19,897 --> 01:08:22,195
<i>I never saw her again.</i>

663
01:08:22,366 --> 01:08:24,163
I swear on my life.

664
01:08:25,035 --> 01:08:27,162
I believe you.

665
01:08:32,209 --> 01:08:33,938
<i>Avada Kedavra!</i>

666
01:08:48,592 --> 01:08:50,082
I thought it wasn't happening anymore.

667
01:08:51,996 --> 01:08:54,430
You can't keep letting him in.

668
01:08:56,500 --> 01:08:59,435
You-Know-Who found
to Gregorovitch.

669
01:08:59,737 --> 01:09:01,295
The wand maker?

670
01:09:01,472 --> 01:09:06,000
He wants something
that Gregorovitch had...

671
01:09:06,176 --> 01:09:07,643
...but I don't know what.

672
01:09:07,811 --> 01:09:13,807
He wants it desperately,
as if his life depended on it.

673
01:09:15,352 --> 01:09:16,876
Nope!

674
01:09:17,054 --> 01:09:19,249
-It comforts him.
-It gets on my nerves.

675
01:09:19,423 --> 01:09:21,653
And are you hoping to hear good news?

676
01:09:24,862 --> 01:09:27,228
Just hope you don't hear bad news.

677
01:09:29,500 --> 01:09:30,933
When will you be able to travel?

678
01:09:34,471 --> 01:09:35,768
I'm doing my best.

679
01:09:35,939 --> 01:09:37,463
It's not enough!

680
01:09:40,210 --> 01:09:42,235
Take it off!

681
01:09:43,013 --> 01:09:45,573
Take it off right now.

682
01:09:56,593 --> 01:09:59,323
-Do you feel better?
-A lot.

683
01:10:03,033 --> 01:10:05,297
We're going to take turns.

684
01:10:34,364 --> 01:10:37,731
<i>Finch admits that his invention
currently has a short.</i>

685
01:10:37,901 --> 01:10:39,368
<i>In other news:</i>

686
01:10:39,536 --> 01:10:42,801
<i>Severus Snape,
the new headmaster of Hogwarts...</i>

687
01:10:42,973 --> 01:10:46,739
<i>...has decreed that all
They must follow the new rules.</i>

688
01:11:14,371 --> 01:11:18,808
<i>Hogwarts bears little resemblance
to the school that Dumbledore ran.</i>

689
01:11:18,976 --> 01:11:22,605
<i>The curriculum is severe,
as the Dark Lord wishes...</i>

690
01:11:23,447 --> 01:11:28,384
<i>...and infractions are punished
by the Death Eaters.</i>

691
01:11:47,871 --> 01:11:49,202
What is that?

692
01:11:58,482 --> 01:12:01,246
What is that smell?

693
01:12:23,707 --> 01:12:25,732
-What are you doing?
-It's heavy.

694
01:12:25,909 --> 01:12:27,501
Should I carry it?

695
01:12:27,678 --> 01:12:30,613
-Yes, thank you.
-Don't be ridiculous. Pick it up!

696
01:12:32,182 --> 01:12:33,206
Dude!

697
01:12:38,322 --> 01:12:40,313
Scavengers.

698
01:12:41,358 --> 01:12:43,792
Your charm worked.

699
01:12:48,832 --> 01:12:52,461
He could smell it. My perfume.

700
01:12:54,671 --> 01:12:56,730
I told you.

701
01:12:57,207 --> 01:12:59,038
Ron doesn't have the strength
to appear.

702
01:12:59,209 --> 01:13:02,940
Then we will go on foot.

703
01:13:03,747 --> 01:13:08,684
Next time though I like it
your perfume, don't put it on.

704
01:13:13,590 --> 01:13:17,458
<i>And now, the names of witches
and missing magicians.</i>

705
01:13:18,328 --> 01:13:20,489
<i>These are confirmed.</i>

706
01:13:21,331 --> 01:13:24,698
<i>Today's list is short.</i>

707
01:13:25,435 --> 01:13:27,494
<i>Jason and Alison Denbright.</i>

708
01:13:28,372 --> 01:13:29,396
Thank you.

709
01:13:29,573 --> 01:13:33,304
<i>Bella, Jake, Charlie and Madge Farley.</i>

710
01:13:33,644 --> 01:13:34,668
<i>Joe Laurie.</i>

711
01:13:35,979 --> 01:13:38,573
<i>Eleanor Sarah Gibbs.</i>

712
01:13:39,750 --> 01:13:43,049
<i>Harry and Bronwyn Trigg.</i>

713
01:13:44,688 --> 01:13:47,714
<i>Rob and Ellie Dowson.</i>

714
01:13:48,825 --> 01:13:51,350
<i>Georgia Clark-Day.</i>

715
01:13:51,929 --> 01:13:54,454
<i>Joshua Flexson.</i>

716
01:13:54,865 --> 01:13:56,355
<i>George Coutas.</i>

717
01:13:57,501 --> 01:14:00,334
<i>Gabriella and Emily Mather.</i>

718
01:14:01,371 --> 01:14:04,465
<i>Jacob and Mimi Erland.</i>

719
01:14:05,542 --> 01:14:07,032
<i>William and Brian Gallagher.</i>

720
01:14:07,210 --> 01:14:09,644
You don't know what you're doing, do you?

721
01:14:12,482 --> 01:14:14,382
None of us know.

722
01:14:16,954 --> 01:14:19,718
<i>Toby and Olivia Gleaves.</i>

723
01:14:20,590 --> 01:14:23,218
<i>Katie and James Killick.</i>

724
01:14:23,393 --> 01:14:25,918
<i>Elsie Valentine Schroeder.</i>

725
01:14:26,964 --> 01:14:29,057
<i>Jennifer Winston.</i>

726
01:14:29,232 --> 01:14:32,326
<i>Tamsin and Lola Hillicker.</i>

727
01:14:33,537 --> 01:14:36,165
<i>Scarlet and Kitty Sharp.</i>

728
01:14:53,452 --> 01:14:55,283
Oh my god!

729
01:14:55,655 --> 01:14:57,282
What?

730
01:14:57,857 --> 01:14:59,882
I'll tell you in a minute.

731
01:15:00,426 --> 01:15:03,122
Maybe you can tell me now.

732
01:15:03,496 --> 01:15:06,522
The Sword of Gryffindor.
It was made by goblins.

733
01:15:06,699 --> 01:15:07,792
Fantastic!

734
01:15:08,868 --> 01:15:11,268
No, you just don't understand.

735
01:15:11,604 --> 01:15:13,970
Rust and dust do not damage the blade.

736
01:15:14,974 --> 01:15:18,341
It only absorbs
which makes it stronger.

737
01:15:20,279 --> 01:15:23,771
You already destroyed a horcrux, right?

738
01:15:23,950 --> 01:15:26,214
The diary in the Chamber of Secrets!

739
01:15:26,386 --> 01:15:29,286
With a basilisk fang.
If you tell me you have...

740
01:15:29,455 --> 01:15:32,913
-...one of those in your bag...
-Don't you understand?

741
01:15:33,092 --> 01:15:36,824
That time you killed the basilisk
with the Sword of Gryffindor.

742
01:15:36,996 --> 01:15:40,523
Its leaf is impregnated
of basilisk venom.

743
01:15:40,700 --> 01:15:42,794
It only absorbs what strengthens it.

744
01:15:42,969 --> 01:15:46,132
-Exactly. That's why...
-Can destroy horcruxes.

745
01:15:46,306 --> 01:15:48,570
That's why Dumbledore bequeathed it to you.

746
01:15:48,741 --> 01:15:53,145
You're brilliant, Hermione, really.

747
01:15:53,312 --> 01:15:57,374
I'm actually extremely logical.
It allows me to ignore extraneous details...

748
01:15:57,550 --> 01:16:00,042
...and perceive what others do not see.

749
01:16:00,220 --> 01:16:02,916
There is only one problem, of course.

750
01:16:08,294 --> 01:16:10,421
They stole the sword.

751
01:16:11,831 --> 01:16:14,356
Yes, I'm still here.

752
01:16:14,867 --> 01:16:18,998
But continue. don't leave me
ruin their fun.

753
01:16:20,373 --> 01:16:24,367
-What do you have?
-What do I have? Nothing.

754
01:16:24,543 --> 01:16:26,443
According to you, everything is fine.

755
01:16:26,613 --> 01:16:30,241
If you have something to say,
don't be shy. Speaks!

756
01:16:30,617 --> 01:16:33,915
Well, I'll talk.
Don't expect me to be grateful...

757
01:16:34,087 --> 01:16:36,611
...because I have to look for something else.

758
01:16:36,789 --> 01:16:39,053
You knew what you were getting into.

759
01:16:39,558 --> 01:16:41,423
I thought I knew.

760
01:16:41,595 --> 01:16:44,620
Sorry, I don't quite understand.

761
01:16:44,798 --> 01:16:48,256
What part of this is not
at the level of what you expected?

762
01:16:48,435 --> 01:16:50,699
Did you think we were going to sleep
in luxury hotels?

763
01:16:50,870 --> 01:16:54,135
Find horcruxes often?
Spending Christmas with your mom?

764
01:16:54,307 --> 01:16:56,137
I was hoping that in all this time...

765
01:16:56,309 --> 01:16:59,745
...we would have already achieved something!
I thought you knew what you were doing!

766
01:16:59,913 --> 01:17:02,313
That Dumbledore taught you useful things.

767
01:17:02,482 --> 01:17:05,679
-That you had a plan.
-I told you everything Dumbledore told me.

768
01:17:05,852 --> 01:17:08,047
And we already found a horcrux.

769
01:17:08,221 --> 01:17:12,089
We can't destroy it,
nor find the missing ones!

770
01:17:12,259 --> 01:17:14,853
Ron. Please take off...

771
01:17:15,395 --> 01:17:17,795
Take off the horcrux.
You talk like that because...

772
01:17:17,963 --> 01:17:21,866
-...you've brought it all day.
-Do you know why I listen to that radio?

773
01:17:22,035 --> 01:17:26,699
To make sure I don't hear the names
from Ginny, Fred, George, or my mom.

774
01:17:26,872 --> 01:17:30,036
And I don't listen to it?
Do you think I don't know what it feels like?

775
01:17:30,210 --> 01:17:31,677
You don't know what it feels like!

776
01:17:31,845 --> 01:17:34,210
Your parents died!
You don't have a family!

777
01:17:35,315 --> 01:17:38,045
-Stop it!
-Okay, go!

778
01:17:38,885 --> 01:17:40,045
Go, then!

779
01:17:47,127 --> 01:17:48,788
Ron!

780
01:17:52,032 --> 01:17:53,828
And you?

781
01:17:55,570 --> 01:17:58,094
Are you coming or staying?

782
01:18:05,212 --> 01:18:08,272
It's okay. I understand.

783
01:18:08,915 --> 01:18:10,883
I saw them the other night.

784
01:18:11,284 --> 01:18:13,718
Ron, that... Nothing happened.

785
01:18:15,856 --> 01:18:17,222
Ron!

786
01:18:20,427 --> 01:18:22,760
Where are you going?

787
01:18:23,763 --> 01:18:25,993
Please come back!

788
01:18:27,467 --> 01:18:29,162
Ron.

789
01:18:33,874 --> 01:18:35,398
Ron!

790
01:19:37,205 --> 01:19:39,832
<i>Salvio Hexia.</i>

791
01:19:43,311 --> 01:19:45,745
<i>Repellum Muggletum.</i>

792
01:19:48,815 --> 01:19:51,249
<i>Salvio Hexia.</i>

793
01:22:58,773 --> 01:23:00,935
I OPEN TO CLOSING

794
01:23:02,210 --> 01:23:03,700
Hermione.

795
01:23:03,879 --> 01:23:06,211
Hermione? You were right!

796
01:23:06,381 --> 01:23:07,938
Snitches have tactile memory...

797
01:23:08,116 --> 01:23:12,746
...but I didn't catch it with my hand.
I almost swallowed it.

798
01:23:18,026 --> 01:23:20,790
-''I open to closure''.
-What does that mean?

799
01:23:20,962 --> 01:23:22,361
I don't know.

800
01:23:24,766 --> 01:23:27,166
I discovered something too.

801
01:23:33,542 --> 01:23:37,000
I thought it was an eye,
but I don't think it is anymore.

802
01:23:37,179 --> 01:23:41,342
It is not a rune and it is not
in the Syllabary of Spells.

803
01:23:41,817 --> 01:23:44,912
Someone drew it in ink.
It is not part of the book.

804
01:23:45,085 --> 01:23:48,749
Luna's father brought that
at Bill and Fleur's wedding.

805
01:23:51,493 --> 01:23:54,792
Why did they draw it?
in a children's book?

806
01:23:57,399 --> 01:23:59,833
I've been thinking.

807
01:24:00,402 --> 01:24:02,495
I want to go to Godric's Hollow.

808
01:24:02,671 --> 01:24:05,731
It's where I was born.
It's where my parents died.

809
01:24:05,907 --> 01:24:09,503
It's right where he waits
that you go, because you care.

810
01:24:09,678 --> 01:24:12,112
It matters to him too, Hermione.

811
01:24:12,281 --> 01:24:14,271
You-Know-Who almost died there.

812
01:24:14,449 --> 01:24:19,114
Isn't that precisely where
would hide a horcrux?

813
01:24:20,088 --> 01:24:22,648
It's dangerous, Harry.

814
01:24:24,259 --> 01:24:28,253
But I have also been
thinking we should go there.

815
01:24:28,430 --> 01:24:30,864
Something else may be hidden there.

816
01:24:31,032 --> 01:24:32,556
What?

817
01:24:33,268 --> 01:24:34,963
The sword.

818
01:24:35,537 --> 01:24:39,338
If Dumbledore wanted you to find it,
hiding it from the Ministry...

819
01:24:39,508 --> 01:24:43,706
...what better place than where
Was the founder of Gryffindor born?

820
01:24:45,047 --> 01:24:46,911
Hermione...

821
01:24:52,153 --> 01:24:54,883
Don't leave again
Let me cut your hair.

822
01:25:16,145 --> 01:25:18,807
we should have used
the Polyjuice Potion.

823
01:25:18,980 --> 01:25:20,504
No.

824
01:25:21,183 --> 01:25:23,378
This is where I was born.

825
01:25:23,718 --> 01:25:26,119
I'm not going to come back as another person.

826
01:25:35,932 --> 01:25:37,797
Good night!

827
01:25:41,971 --> 01:25:44,735
I think it's Christmas Eve.

828
01:25:46,242 --> 01:25:47,970
Listen.

829
01:25:53,249 --> 01:25:56,082
Do you think they are there?

830
01:25:56,519 --> 01:25:58,509
My mom and dad?

831
01:26:04,460 --> 01:26:06,724
Yes, I think so.

832
01:26:43,299 --> 01:26:46,359
''Ignotus Peverell''.

833
01:26:48,437 --> 01:26:50,064
Harry?

834
01:27:27,943 --> 01:27:30,138
Merry Christmas, Hermione.

835
01:27:31,447 --> 01:27:33,678
Merry Christmas, Harry.

836
01:27:53,536 --> 01:27:58,941
There is someone watching us,
next to the church.

837
01:28:09,653 --> 01:28:11,483
I think I know who it is.

838
01:28:13,356 --> 01:28:14,788
I don't like this.

839
01:28:14,958 --> 01:28:19,986
She knew Dumbledore.
Maybe he has the sword.

840
01:28:38,848 --> 01:28:40,476
This is where they died.

841
01:28:48,058 --> 01:28:50,525
This is where he murdered them.

842
01:29:03,039 --> 01:29:04,972
You are Bathilda, right?

843
01:29:10,579 --> 01:29:12,673
Leave it to me.

844
01:29:36,807 --> 01:29:40,709
Miss Bagshot, who is this man?

845
01:29:52,322 --> 01:29:53,983
Harry.

846
01:29:58,028 --> 01:29:59,893
<i>Lumos.</i>

847
01:30:20,350 --> 01:30:22,545
LIFE & LIES
BY ALBUS DUMBLEDORE

848
01:31:40,264 --> 01:31:41,288
Harry!

849
01:32:32,115 --> 01:32:33,174
<i>Confringo!</i>

850
01:33:15,926 --> 01:33:18,053
Do you feel better?

851
01:33:21,133 --> 01:33:23,600
This time you really shined.

852
01:33:23,769 --> 01:33:25,861
The Forest of Dean.

853
01:33:26,837 --> 01:33:31,206
I came here with my parents,
many years ago.

854
01:33:31,842 --> 01:33:33,969
It's just as I remember it.

855
01:33:34,378 --> 01:33:38,314
The trees, the river. All.

856
01:33:38,616 --> 01:33:41,449
As if nothing had changed.

857
01:33:42,686 --> 01:33:45,679
It's not true. Everything has changed.

858
01:33:46,657 --> 01:33:50,458
If I brought my parents,
They wouldn't recognize anything.

859
01:33:52,563 --> 01:33:56,693
Neither the trees, nor the river...

860
01:33:58,469 --> 01:34:00,596
...not even to me.

861
01:34:05,743 --> 01:34:08,542
Maybe we should
stay here, Harry.

862
01:34:10,549 --> 01:34:12,676
Grow old.

863
01:34:18,689 --> 01:34:21,989
You wanted to know who he was
the boy in the photo.

864
01:34:22,727 --> 01:34:23,818
I found out.

865
01:34:24,996 --> 01:34:27,395
It's Gellert Grindelwald.

866
01:34:34,338 --> 01:34:37,740
It's the thief that I saw
in Gregorovitch's shop.

867
01:34:37,909 --> 01:34:41,174
By the way,
where is my wand?

868
01:34:42,513 --> 01:34:44,914
Where's my wand, Hermione?

869
01:34:53,557 --> 01:34:58,052
Leaving Godric's Hollow,
I swore and it bounced back.

870
01:35:00,798 --> 01:35:02,027
Forgive me.

871
01:35:02,700 --> 01:35:05,329
-I tried to fix it, but they are different.
-That's done, chest.

872
01:35:07,305 --> 01:35:11,264
Leave me yours.
Get in and warm up.

873
01:35:11,676 --> 01:35:14,008
And leave me the locket.

874
01:35:26,558 --> 01:35:27,923
<i>Trust me.</i>

875
01:36:53,678 --> 01:36:55,306
<i>Lumos.</i>

876
01:37:36,389 --> 01:37:37,753
<i>Accio sword.</i>

877
01:37:43,595 --> 01:37:45,495
<i>Diffindo.</i>

878
01:39:25,932 --> 01:39:29,094
-Hermione?
-You're crazy?

879
01:39:30,302 --> 01:39:31,861
Was it you?

880
01:39:32,037 --> 01:39:35,803
Well, yes. It's a bit obvious.

881
01:39:35,976 --> 01:39:37,772
Did you create the deer?

882
01:39:38,345 --> 01:39:42,007
-No, I thought it was you.
-No, my Patronus is a deer.

883
01:39:42,181 --> 01:39:44,376
True, yes. Antlers.

884
01:39:47,553 --> 01:39:50,717
Well, Ron. Do it.

885
01:39:51,690 --> 01:39:55,421
I can't.
It affects me more than it affects you.

886
01:39:55,961 --> 01:39:58,589
-More reason to destroy it.
-No. Can't.

887
01:39:58,764 --> 01:39:59,993
Why did you come?

888
01:40:01,400 --> 01:40:03,460
Why did you come back?

889
01:40:11,043 --> 01:40:15,174
I'm going to talk to him to get him to open up.
When it opens, don't hesitate.

890
01:40:15,781 --> 01:40:18,307
I don't know what's inside,
but he is going to defend himself.

891
01:40:18,485 --> 01:40:21,181
That piece of Riddle from the Diary attacked me.

892
01:40:23,657 --> 01:40:25,283
Good.

893
01:40:26,126 --> 01:40:27,684
One...

894
01:40:28,360 --> 01:40:29,419
...two...

895
01:40:30,095 --> 01:40:31,996
...three.

896
01:40:42,242 --> 01:40:47,339
<i>I have seen your heart and it is mine.</i>

897
01:40:49,950 --> 01:40:53,851
<i>I have seen your dreams,
Ronald Weasley...</i>

898
01:40:54,020 --> 01:40:56,420
<i>...and I have seen your fears.</i>

899
01:40:58,124 --> 01:41:02,287
<i>Illly loved by your mother,
who longed for a daughter.</i>

900
01:41:02,929 --> 01:41:07,922
<i>Badly loved by your girlfriend
who prefers your friend.</i>

901
01:41:08,100 --> 01:41:10,831
Ron, kill him!

902
01:41:17,276 --> 01:41:19,973
We were better off without you.

903
01:41:20,480 --> 01:41:22,208
Happier without you.

904
01:41:22,382 --> 01:41:27,752
Who can look at you
compared to Harry Potter?

905
01:41:28,989 --> 01:41:32,322
Who are you,
compared to The Chosen One?

906
01:41:32,492 --> 01:41:33,651
Ron, he's lying!

907
01:41:33,826 --> 01:41:36,819
Your mother would have me
preferred to me as a son.

908
01:41:36,997 --> 01:41:39,990
What woman is going to love you?

909
01:41:40,200 --> 01:41:43,363
You are nothing.

910
01:41:43,537 --> 01:41:44,663
Nothing.

911
01:41:45,438 --> 01:41:49,465
Nothing, compared to him.

912
01:42:40,026 --> 01:42:41,687
Think...

913
01:42:42,596 --> 01:42:44,690
...only three are missing.

914
01:42:47,734 --> 01:42:49,463
Hermione?

915
01:42:51,739 --> 01:42:53,467
Hermione?

916
01:42:58,012 --> 01:42:59,945
Is everything okay?

917
01:43:00,580 --> 01:43:05,244
It's okay.
Honestly, it's better than good.

918
01:43:09,690 --> 01:43:11,282
Hello.

919
01:43:15,528 --> 01:43:21,729
You are a complete idiot,
Ronald Weasley!

920
01:43:21,901 --> 01:43:25,565
Will you show up here later
of weeks and you say ''Hello''?

921
01:43:27,774 --> 01:43:30,505
-Where is my wand, Harry?
-I don't know.

922
01:43:30,677 --> 01:43:32,941
-Give me my wand!
-I don't have it!

923
01:43:33,114 --> 01:43:36,948
-Why does he have your wand?
-It doesn't matter why he has my wand!

924
01:43:39,219 --> 01:43:40,448
What is that?

925
01:43:43,391 --> 01:43:44,415
You destroyed it.

926
01:43:47,727 --> 01:43:51,686
And how come you have
the Sword of Gryffindor?

927
01:43:52,099 --> 01:43:54,067
It's a long story.

928
01:43:57,238 --> 01:44:01,334
-Don't think this changes anything.
-Of course not.

929
01:44:01,508 --> 01:44:04,773
I only destroyed one horcrux.
Why would anything change?

930
01:44:04,944 --> 01:44:09,006
I wanted to come back as soon as I left.

931
01:44:09,182 --> 01:44:12,619
-I didn't know how to find them.
-How did you find us?

932
01:44:12,787 --> 01:44:15,847
With this. It doesn't just turn off lights.

933
01:44:16,023 --> 01:44:20,926
I don't know how it works. But at Christmas
I was sleeping in a pub...

934
01:44:21,094 --> 01:44:23,528
...hiding from some scavengers.

935
01:44:23,964 --> 01:44:25,226
And I heard it.

936
01:44:25,633 --> 01:44:27,066
''The''?

937
01:44:28,402 --> 01:44:30,336
A voice.

938
01:44:31,939 --> 01:44:33,133
Your voice, Hermione.

939
01:44:34,308 --> 01:44:35,935
Coming out of it.

940
01:44:36,110 --> 01:44:39,944
-And what exactly did I say?
-My name.

941
01:44:40,548 --> 01:44:42,572
Just my name.

942
01:44:43,350 --> 01:44:45,442
Like a whisper.

943
01:44:47,421 --> 01:44:53,417
I grabbed it, I clicked it
and a ball of light appeared.

944
01:44:53,894 --> 01:44:55,327
And then I knew.

945
01:44:55,896 --> 01:45:00,526
And of course
floated towards me, the ball of light.

946
01:45:02,237 --> 01:45:06,434
It went straight to my chest
and it pierced me. Here.

947
01:45:07,642 --> 01:45:11,634
I knew it was going to take me where
I needed to go and I disappeared...

948
01:45:11,812 --> 01:45:14,076
...and I came to this hill.

949
01:45:14,615 --> 01:45:17,140
It was dark.
I didn't know where I was.

950
01:45:17,685 --> 01:45:20,519
I was just waiting
for one of you to arrive.

951
01:45:21,423 --> 01:45:22,946
And so it was.

952
01:45:40,375 --> 01:45:43,275
I like flames
What does Hermione do?

953
01:45:47,314 --> 01:45:49,874
How long will it be
angry with me?

954
01:45:51,419 --> 01:45:54,751
Keep talking about the ball
of light in your heart...

955
01:45:54,923 --> 01:45:56,356
...and it's going to pass.

956
01:45:56,525 --> 01:45:59,254
It was true, until the last word.

957
01:46:01,062 --> 01:46:03,428
It's going to seem crazy to you.

958
01:46:03,898 --> 01:46:08,268
I think that's why Dumbledore
He left me the deluminator.

959
01:46:08,769 --> 01:46:13,764
I knew I would need it to come back.
and that she would guide me.

960
01:46:16,645 --> 01:46:19,374
I just realized,
you need a wand.

961
01:46:19,547 --> 01:46:22,039
-Yes.
-I have one here.

962
01:46:22,316 --> 01:46:24,911
It's blackthorn.
25 centimeters.

963
01:46:25,085 --> 01:46:28,681
It's nothing special, but it works.

964
01:46:29,123 --> 01:46:31,922
I took it from a scavenger
two weeks ago.

965
01:46:32,427 --> 01:46:36,261
Don't tell Hermione, but they are
a little stupid, the scavengers.

966
01:46:36,530 --> 01:46:39,466
This one was half a troll because of how it smelled.

967
01:46:39,633 --> 01:46:40,658
<i>Engorgio.</i>

968
01:46:40,836 --> 01:46:42,996
<i>-Reducio!
-What's going on there?</i>

969
01:46:43,170 --> 01:46:44,432
-Nothing!
-Nothing!

970
01:46:46,807 --> 01:46:48,435
We need to talk.

971
01:46:49,244 --> 01:46:50,438
Yes, it's okay.

972
01:46:57,419 --> 01:47:00,946
-I want to go see Xenophilius Lovegood.
-Sorry?

973
01:47:02,723 --> 01:47:04,351
Do you see this?

974
01:47:04,526 --> 01:47:08,394
It is a letter that Dumbledore
he wrote to Grindelwald. Look at the signature.

975
01:47:09,630 --> 01:47:11,825
There's the symbol again.

976
01:47:12,766 --> 01:47:14,893
It appears all the time.

977
01:47:15,070 --> 01:47:19,439
<i>In Beedle, the Bard, in the
Godric's Hollow Cemetery.</i>

978
01:47:20,275 --> 01:47:22,139
It was there too.

979
01:47:22,309 --> 01:47:25,905
-Where?
-Outside Gregorovitch's shop.

980
01:47:26,348 --> 01:47:27,576
What does it mean?

981
01:47:27,749 --> 01:47:32,551
You have no idea where it is
the next horcrux and neither do I.

982
01:47:34,256 --> 01:47:37,191
But this, this means something.

983
01:47:37,525 --> 01:47:40,926
-I'm sure.
-Yeah. Hermione is right.

984
01:47:41,963 --> 01:47:44,056
We must go see Lovegood.

985
01:47:44,566 --> 01:47:48,296
You have to vote.
Who is in favor?

986
01:48:12,127 --> 01:48:14,755
You're not still mad at him, are you?

987
01:48:15,063 --> 01:48:17,327
I'm always angry with him.

988
01:48:20,101 --> 01:48:21,591
Moon.

989
01:48:21,770 --> 01:48:23,465
-Moon.
-Moon.

990
01:48:23,639 --> 01:48:26,129
BE CAREFUL WITH THE
DIRECTIONAL PLUMS

991
01:48:29,577 --> 01:48:30,977
THE NICKY PICKER
Editor X. LOVEGOOD

992
01:48:31,147 --> 01:48:33,980
''Be careful with the
steerable plums''.

993
01:48:43,024 --> 01:48:45,720
What do you want? Who are they?

994
01:48:46,027 --> 01:48:47,051
What do they want?

995
01:48:47,229 --> 01:48:51,825
Mr. Lovegood. I am Harry Potter.
We met a few months ago.

996
01:48:55,837 --> 01:48:57,737
Can we come in?

997
01:49:01,510 --> 01:49:04,103
-Where is Luna?
-Moon?

998
01:49:05,381 --> 01:49:07,348
He will be back soon.

999
01:49:20,863 --> 01:49:22,921
How may I be of service to you, Mr. Potter?

1000
01:49:23,765 --> 01:49:26,792
The truth is, it's about...

1001
01:49:27,802 --> 01:49:32,330
...of something that was hanging
of the neck at the wedding. A symbol.

1002
01:49:33,876 --> 01:49:35,775
Are you referring to this?

1003
01:49:36,178 --> 01:49:37,770
Yes.

1004
01:49:38,079 --> 01:49:39,944
That precisely.

1005
01:49:40,615 --> 01:49:44,575
We were curious. What is it?

1006
01:49:44,754 --> 01:49:46,584
What is it?

1007
01:49:46,755 --> 01:49:49,725
It is the sign of the Relics
Of Death, of course.

1008
01:49:49,891 --> 01:49:50,983
Of what?

1009
01:49:51,160 --> 01:49:53,219
From the Deathly Hallows.

1010
01:49:53,395 --> 01:49:56,489
I guess you know
''The Fable of the Three Brothers''.

1011
01:49:56,664 --> 01:49:58,155
-Yes.
-No.

1012
01:50:03,506 --> 01:50:05,269
I have it here.

1013
01:50:16,519 --> 01:50:18,146
''Once upon a time there were three brothers...

1014
01:50:18,320 --> 01:50:22,723
...who were traveling along a road
at dusk."

1015
01:50:22,892 --> 01:50:25,622
At midnight. my mom
He always said ''at midnight''.

1016
01:50:30,634 --> 01:50:34,501
''At dusk'' is fine.
Better, in fact.

1017
01:50:36,772 --> 01:50:38,638
Do you want to read it?

1018
01:50:38,808 --> 01:50:41,003
No, it's okay.

1019
01:50:42,912 --> 01:50:44,847
<i>''Once upon a time there were three brothers...</i>

1020
01:50:45,014 --> 01:50:50,213
<i>...who were traveling alone
along a path at dusk.</i>

1021
01:50:52,089 --> 01:50:57,390
<i>They came to a river too
treacherous to pass it.</i>

1022
01:50:57,726 --> 01:50:59,592
<i>Being versed in magic...</i>

1023
01:50:59,762 --> 01:51:04,928
<i>...the three brothers waved their wands
and they made a bridge.</i>

1024
01:51:06,269 --> 01:51:08,361
<i>But before we go...</i>

1025
01:51:08,538 --> 01:51:12,634
<i>...blocked their way
a hooded figure.</i>

1026
01:51:12,908 --> 01:51:16,776
<i>It was Death.
And she felt cheated.</i>

1027
01:51:16,946 --> 01:51:20,006
<i>Normally travelers
They were drowning in the river.</i>

1028
01:51:20,182 --> 01:51:22,241
<i>But Death was cunning.</i>

1029
01:51:22,885 --> 01:51:25,878
<i>He congratulated the three brothers
for its magic...</i>

1030
01:51:26,055 --> 01:51:31,322
<i>...and he said they deserved
a prize for having evaded it.</i>

1031
01:51:31,894 --> 01:51:36,456
<i>The oldest asked for a more powerful wand
than all those that existed.</i>

1032
01:51:36,633 --> 01:51:41,229
<i>Death made him one of a tree
of elderberry that was nearby.</i>

1033
01:51:42,639 --> 01:51:46,938
<i>The second brother wanted to humiliate
to Death even more.</i>

1034
01:51:47,109 --> 01:51:51,546
<i>He asked for the power to call
his loved ones from the grave.</i>

1035
01:51:51,981 --> 01:51:56,282
<i>Death took a stone
from the river and offered it to him.</i>

1036
01:51:57,019 --> 01:52:00,978
<i>Finally, Death
He headed to the third.</i>

1037
01:52:02,192 --> 01:52:03,625
<i>A humble man...</i>

1038
01:52:03,792 --> 01:52:07,990
<i>...he asked her for something that would allow him
get away from that place...</i>

1039
01:52:08,164 --> 01:52:11,327
<i>...without Death following him.</i>

1040
01:52:12,434 --> 01:52:18,304
<i>This was how Death gave him
his Cloak of Invisibility.</i>

1041
01:52:21,678 --> 01:52:24,613
<i>The first brother traveled
to a distant town...</i>

1042
01:52:24,781 --> 01:52:26,873
<i>...where, Elder Wand in hand...</i>

1043
01:52:27,050 --> 01:52:30,816
<i>...he killed a magician with whom
He had fought before.</i>

1044
01:52:33,022 --> 01:52:36,549
<i>Intoxicated with the power that
the Elder Wand had given him...</i>

1045
01:52:36,726 --> 01:52:39,820
<i>...bragged about being invincible.</i>

1046
01:52:42,831 --> 01:52:46,289
<i>But that night another magician
he stole her wand...</i>

1047
01:52:46,468 --> 01:52:49,597
<i>...and, in the process, he slit his throat.</i>

1048
01:52:49,806 --> 01:52:53,241
<i>And so Death appropriated
of the first brother.</i>

1049
01:52:53,976 --> 01:52:55,945
<i>The second one went home...</i>

1050
01:52:56,111 --> 01:52:59,081
<i>...where he took the stone
and he turned it three times in his hand.</i>

1051
01:52:59,248 --> 01:53:03,709
<i>The girl he hoped to marry
before his untimely death...</i>

1052
01:53:03,886 --> 01:53:06,253
<i>...appeared before him.</i>

1053
01:53:06,756 --> 01:53:12,058
<i>But soon she became sad and cold,
for he no longer belonged to the mortal world.</i>

1054
01:53:12,229 --> 01:53:13,855
<i>Crazed by a longing
hopeless...</i>

1055
01:53:14,030 --> 01:53:17,329
<i>...the second brother
He committed suicide to reach her.</i>

1056
01:53:18,535 --> 01:53:21,629
<i>And so Death took
to the second brother.</i>

1057
01:53:21,804 --> 01:53:23,432
<i>But on the third...</i>

1058
01:53:23,607 --> 01:53:27,838
<i>...Death searched for him for many years,
but he could never find it.</i>

1059
01:53:28,011 --> 01:53:30,912
<i>Only upon reaching an age
advanced, the little brother...</i>

1060
01:53:31,082 --> 01:53:35,348
<i>...removed the Cloak of Invisibility
and he gave it to his son.</i>

1061
01:53:36,586 --> 01:53:40,715
<i>He greeted Death as
to an old friend and went with her...</i>

1062
01:53:40,891 --> 01:53:44,690
<i>...starting from this life
as equals''.</i>

1063
01:53:46,129 --> 01:53:50,623
There you have it. Those are
the Deathly Hallows.

1064
01:53:52,036 --> 01:53:55,095
Excuse me, I don't quite understand.

1065
01:54:13,790 --> 01:54:15,052
The Elder Wand.

1066
01:54:16,192 --> 01:54:19,856
The most powerful wand
that has existed.

1067
01:54:30,240 --> 01:54:32,539
The Stone of Resurrection.

1068
01:54:43,420 --> 01:54:47,186
The Cloak of Invisibility.

1069
01:54:49,225 --> 01:54:52,354
Together, they form
the Deathly Hallows.

1070
01:54:52,630 --> 01:54:58,090
Together, they make it one
master of Death.

1071
01:55:03,307 --> 01:55:06,969
That symbol was on
a tomb in Godric's Hollow.

1072
01:55:08,845 --> 01:55:10,710
Do the Peverells have anything to do with...

1073
01:55:10,880 --> 01:55:13,543
...with the Deathly Hallows?

1074
01:55:15,885 --> 01:55:19,651
Ignotus, excuse me, and your brothers,
Cadmus and Antioch...

1075
01:55:19,824 --> 01:55:22,485
...were the original owners
of the Relics...

1076
01:55:22,659 --> 01:55:25,823
...and inspired the story.

1077
01:55:27,697 --> 01:55:30,189
Their tea got cold.

1078
01:55:31,402 --> 01:55:33,392
I'll be right back.

1079
01:55:37,308 --> 01:55:38,797
Let's go.

1080
01:55:38,975 --> 01:55:41,843
I'm not going to take any more of that,
hot or cold.

1081
01:55:48,151 --> 01:55:50,120
Thank you, sir.

1082
01:55:51,020 --> 01:55:54,047
-He forgot the water.
-The water?

1083
01:55:54,225 --> 01:55:55,658
For tea.

1084
01:55:55,826 --> 01:55:58,386
Did I forget her?

1085
01:56:00,331 --> 01:56:02,492
What a fool!

1086
01:56:04,101 --> 01:56:06,365
It doesn't matter.
We have to go.

1087
01:56:06,537 --> 01:56:08,698
They can't leave!

1088
01:56:12,810 --> 01:56:14,505
Sir?

1089
01:56:21,885 --> 01:56:24,479
You are my only hope.

1090
01:56:28,359 --> 01:56:32,727
They were angry because
I had been writing.

1091
01:56:35,766 --> 01:56:37,893
So they took her away.

1092
01:56:39,370 --> 01:56:42,134
They took my Moon.

1093
01:56:43,840 --> 01:56:45,468
To my Moon.

1094
01:56:57,955 --> 01:57:00,856
But they love you.

1095
01:57:03,093 --> 01:57:05,152
Who took her?

1096
01:57:10,302 --> 01:57:11,564
Voldemort.

1097
01:57:22,214 --> 01:57:24,511
Stop! I already have it!

1098
01:57:41,800 --> 01:57:45,702
Treacherous scoundrel!
Can't we trust anyone?

1099
01:57:45,870 --> 01:57:48,169
They kidnapped her because she supported me.

1100
01:57:48,339 --> 01:57:50,466
I was desperate.

1101
01:57:51,008 --> 01:57:53,203
I'm going to do the incantations.

1102
01:58:04,889 --> 01:58:06,322
Hello, beautiful.

1103
01:58:11,796 --> 01:58:15,424
Don't just stand there!
Grab them!

1104
01:59:26,671 --> 01:59:28,160
<i>Harry!</i>

1105
01:59:28,339 --> 01:59:31,309
<i>Tell me, Grindelwald.
Tell me where it is.</i>

1106
01:59:31,910 --> 01:59:35,971
<i>Grindelwald. Grindelwald.
Grindelwald.</i>

1107
01:59:36,715 --> 01:59:40,173
Hello, Tom.
I knew you were going to come one day...

1108
01:59:40,651 --> 01:59:44,611
...but I'm sure you already know
I don't have what you're looking for.

1109
01:59:45,256 --> 01:59:48,282
Tell me, Grindelwald.
Tell me where it is.

1110
01:59:48,460 --> 01:59:49,825
Tell me who owns it.

1111
01:59:50,028 --> 01:59:55,125
The Elder Wand
lies with him, of course...

1112
01:59:55,300 --> 01:59:57,565
...buried in the ground.

1113
01:59:58,503 --> 01:59:59,834
With Dumbledore.

1114
02:00:08,881 --> 02:00:10,745
The Relics exist.

1115
02:00:10,915 --> 02:00:14,715
But just look for one,
the last one. He knows where it is.

1116
02:00:14,887 --> 02:00:18,721
You'll have it tonight.
You-Know-Who found it.

1117
02:00:18,891 --> 02:00:21,358
-Don't touch her!
-Leave it!

1118
02:00:21,527 --> 02:00:24,086
Your boyfriend is going to be much worse...

1119
02:00:24,262 --> 02:00:28,494
...if he doesn't learn to behave.

1120
02:00:30,235 --> 02:00:31,726
What happened to you, ugly?

1121
02:00:33,439 --> 02:00:35,304
No, not you.

1122
02:00:36,709 --> 02:00:39,768
-What's your name?
-Dudley. Vernon Dudley.

1123
02:00:39,944 --> 02:00:41,742
See if it is there.

1124
02:00:43,749 --> 02:00:46,081
And you, precious?

1125
02:00:49,388 --> 02:00:51,378
What's your name?

1126
02:00:52,824 --> 02:00:56,885
I'm Penelope Clearwater, mixed race.

1127
02:00:59,998 --> 02:01:01,933
There's no Vernon Dudley here.

1128
02:01:03,001 --> 02:01:06,233
Did you hear that, ugly?
The list says you're lying.

1129
02:01:06,404 --> 02:01:08,635
Why don't you want
let us know your name?

1130
02:01:08,808 --> 02:01:11,469
The list is wrong.
I already told you who I am.

1131
02:01:27,426 --> 02:01:29,519
A change of plan.

1132
02:01:30,595 --> 02:01:33,860
We are not going to take them to the Ministry.

1133
02:02:13,539 --> 02:02:17,168
Call Draco.

1134
02:02:21,646 --> 02:02:23,205
Well?

1135
02:02:26,318 --> 02:02:30,846
-I can't be sure.
-Draco, look at him carefully, son.

1136
02:02:31,857 --> 02:02:36,920
If we give him Potter
to the Dark Lord...

1137
02:02:37,096 --> 02:02:42,329
...all will be forgiven.
Everything will be as before, you understand?

1138
02:02:42,501 --> 02:02:46,733
We will not forget who
You caught it, didn't you, Mr. Malfoy?

1139
02:02:46,906 --> 02:02:49,238
Do you dare to talk to me like that
in my house?

1140
02:02:49,408 --> 02:02:51,205
Lucius!

1141
02:02:54,113 --> 02:02:57,947
Don't be shy. Come closer.

1142
02:02:59,451 --> 02:03:04,218
If it's not the person we think
and we call it, it kills us all.

1143
02:03:04,390 --> 02:03:07,188
We need to be sure.

1144
02:03:07,493 --> 02:03:10,394
-What does he have on his face?
-Yes, what do you have?

1145
02:03:10,564 --> 02:03:13,896
This is how it was when we grabbed it.
Maybe he ate something in the forest.

1146
02:03:14,067 --> 02:03:17,764
Or ran into a Stinging Haunt.
Was it you, dear?

1147
02:03:22,876 --> 02:03:25,640
In his wand we will see which
It was his last incantation.

1148
02:03:28,648 --> 02:03:30,342
I grabbed you.

1149
02:03:32,886 --> 02:03:34,614
What is that?

1150
02:03:36,556 --> 02:03:38,147
Where did you get it from?

1151
02:03:38,324 --> 02:03:41,816
It was in his bag when
we register it. Now it's mine.

1152
02:03:45,565 --> 02:03:46,895
Is she crazy?

1153
02:03:55,208 --> 02:03:58,040
Go away! Out!

1154
02:04:03,682 --> 02:04:07,847
Cissy, lock up the boys!
in the basement!

1155
02:04:08,021 --> 02:04:13,390
I want to have a little chat
with this one, from girl to girl!

1156
02:04:22,435 --> 02:04:25,528
What are we going to do? we can't
leave Hermione with her!

1157
02:04:25,705 --> 02:04:27,070
Ron?

1158
02:04:32,278 --> 02:04:33,837
Harry?

1159
02:04:39,552 --> 02:04:41,109
Moon?

1160
02:04:41,720 --> 02:04:45,885
That sword was in my vault,
at Gringotts. How did you get it?

1161
02:04:46,059 --> 02:04:49,186
What else did they take?
you and your friends from my vault?

1162
02:04:49,361 --> 02:04:54,732
I didn't take anything. Please!
I didn't take anything!

1163
02:04:54,900 --> 02:04:56,960
I don't believe you.

1164
02:05:02,008 --> 02:05:03,100
We need to do something!

1165
02:05:03,275 --> 02:05:07,303
There's no way out of here!
We tried everything! He is delighted.

1166
02:05:07,480 --> 02:05:10,176
-Please, please!
-Be quiet!

1167
02:05:10,350 --> 02:05:12,147
You're bleeding, Harry.

1168
02:05:12,318 --> 02:05:14,343
It's weird keeping that in there.

1169
02:05:23,596 --> 02:05:24,721
Help us.

1170
02:05:30,504 --> 02:05:32,403
-Let her go!
-Be quiet. Move.

1171
02:05:33,740 --> 02:05:37,937
You, elf. Come with me.

1172
02:05:57,764 --> 02:05:59,095
Dobby?

1173
02:05:59,966 --> 02:06:01,365
What are you doing here?

1174
02:06:01,534 --> 02:06:03,798
Dobby is coming to the rescue!
to Harry Potter, of course!

1175
02:06:03,970 --> 02:06:06,438
Dobby will always help you
to Harry Potter!

1176
02:06:06,606 --> 02:06:10,201
Can you appear and disappear
from here? Can you take us with you?

1177
02:06:10,378 --> 02:06:12,141
Sure. I am an elf.

1178
02:06:12,946 --> 02:06:14,811
I believe him.

1179
02:06:15,048 --> 02:06:17,414
Take Luna and Mr. Ollivander...

1180
02:06:17,584 --> 02:06:20,018
To the shelter on the outskirts
by Tinworth.

1181
02:06:20,387 --> 02:06:21,411
Trust me.

1182
02:06:22,222 --> 02:06:23,655
When you're ready, sir.

1183
02:06:24,357 --> 02:06:27,053
''Sir''?
I like her a lot!

1184
02:06:31,998 --> 02:06:35,297
See you at the top of the stairs
in ten seconds.

1185
02:06:51,552 --> 02:06:53,781
Whose wand gets it?

1186
02:06:56,524 --> 02:07:00,516
I'm just going to ask you
once again, goblin.

1187
02:07:00,694 --> 02:07:04,094
Think very carefully
before answering.

1188
02:07:04,465 --> 02:07:06,022
I don't know.

1189
02:07:06,200 --> 02:07:09,397
Don't you know?
Why didn't you do your job?

1190
02:07:09,570 --> 02:07:12,800
Who broke into my vault?

1191
02:07:14,075 --> 02:07:18,512
Who stole it?
Who stole it?

1192
02:07:18,678 --> 02:07:22,706
When I was there,
the sword was in the vault.

1193
02:07:22,883 --> 02:07:25,317
mudblood

1194
02:07:25,485 --> 02:07:28,683
Maybe he walked out!

1195
02:07:28,855 --> 02:07:31,289
There is no safer place
than Gringotts.

1196
02:07:31,458 --> 02:07:32,891
Liar!

1197
02:07:34,829 --> 02:07:38,230
Count yourself lucky, leprechaun.

1198
02:07:40,668 --> 02:07:44,069
She's not going to do so well.

1199
02:07:44,238 --> 02:07:46,001
No way!

1200
02:07:46,740 --> 02:07:47,967
<i>Expelliarmus!</i>

1201
02:07:49,409 --> 02:07:50,502
<i>Fainting!</i>

1202
02:07:54,648 --> 02:07:56,013
Stop!

1203
02:07:57,184 --> 02:07:58,741
Drop your wands!

1204
02:08:01,622 --> 02:08:02,646
Release them!

1205
02:08:04,158 --> 02:08:05,591
Pick them up, Draco! Now!

1206
02:08:06,460 --> 02:08:10,589
Just look.
Look what we have here.

1207
02:08:12,199 --> 02:08:13,688
It's Harry Potter.

1208
02:08:14,468 --> 02:08:20,840
It's handsome and like new,
ready for the Dark Lord.

1209
02:08:21,008 --> 02:08:23,033
Call him.

1210
02:08:26,780 --> 02:08:28,576
Call him!

1211
02:09:03,784 --> 02:09:05,615
<i>Fainting!</i>

1212
02:09:06,387 --> 02:09:08,082
Stupid elf!

1213
02:09:08,255 --> 02:09:11,281
-You could have killed me!
-Dobby never wanted to kill!

1214
02:09:11,459 --> 02:09:15,485
Dobby just wanted to maim
or seriously injure.

1215
02:09:17,798 --> 02:09:21,131
How dare you take away
his wand to a witch!

1216
02:09:21,302 --> 02:09:24,295
How dare you
challenge your masters!

1217
02:09:24,471 --> 02:09:27,599
Dobby doesn't have a master.

1218
02:09:27,776 --> 02:09:30,266
Dobby is a free elf.

1219
02:09:30,444 --> 02:09:35,404
And Dobby has come to save
to Harry Potter and his friends!

1220
02:10:05,247 --> 02:10:06,907
Hermione.

1221
02:10:07,081 --> 02:10:09,573
You're fine. We are safe.

1222
02:10:09,750 --> 02:10:11,775
We are all safe.

1223
02:10:12,654 --> 02:10:14,849
Harry Potter.

1224
02:10:18,593 --> 02:10:20,424
Dobby!

1225
02:10:30,938 --> 02:10:33,999
Dobby. No. Nothing else lasts.

1226
02:10:34,175 --> 02:10:38,509
Hold on. Look.
Just hold on, okay?

1227
02:10:38,680 --> 02:10:40,738
We're going to fix you.

1228
02:10:41,182 --> 02:10:43,911
I'm sure Hermione has something.

1229
02:10:44,085 --> 02:10:46,417
In your bag. Hermione?

1230
02:10:48,056 --> 02:10:49,387
Hermione?

1231
02:10:51,593 --> 02:10:54,720
Help me!

1232
02:10:57,299 --> 02:11:00,427
What a beautiful place...

1233
02:11:02,604 --> 02:11:04,868
...to be with friends.

1234
02:11:06,674 --> 02:11:12,079
Dobby is happy
to be with your friend...

1235
02:11:14,481 --> 02:11:16,915
...Harry Potter.

1236
02:11:37,706 --> 02:11:40,105
We should close his eyes.

1237
02:11:40,342 --> 02:11:42,367
Don't you think?

1238
02:11:47,482 --> 02:11:48,882
Ya.

1239
02:11:49,351 --> 02:11:51,785
He could be asleep now.

1240
02:12:07,102 --> 02:12:09,161
I want to bury him.

1241
02:12:10,205 --> 02:12:13,767
A dignified burial. No magic.
